<title>JAPAN: Japan end-Jan kerosene stockpiles up 30.2% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan end-Jan kerosene stockpiles up 30.2% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's kerosene stockpiles stood at 3.4 million kilolitres (kl) as of the end of January, up 30.2 percent from a year earlier but down 17 percent from a month earlier, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Sales of kerosene, used in Japan to heat houses, peak during the four-month period from November to February.</p>
</text>
